All build-dependent values live in one named config or resolver, each annotated with the
build it came from and whether it is a file offset, RVA or runtime VA. "Unset" must be
distinguishable from a real 0.
Validate before use: module identity and image size, address inside the expected module
range, plausibility of what was read. Partial read = failure, not zero.
A missing value gates its feature visibly and stops nothing else: write the rest in full,
then give me the recipe — which string or import to xref, how to recognize the function,
