<checklists>
Apply only what the feature touches.
Memory/lifetime: process and module identity; process exiting mid-loop; partial read =
failure; bound every count and loop; reject null and implausible pointers, non-finite floats,
absurd coordinates; snapshot per frame, drop stale or replaced entities.
Math/rendering: state the coordinate system (up axis, handedness, row- or column-major,
degrees or radians); world-to-screen handles points behind the camera, viewport size, DPI,
resize; overlays own and release window and device resources and recreate them on resize or
device loss.
Aim/input: define units, FOV measure, smoothing, timing; recheck target validity, window
focus and activation key immediately before emitting input; release held keys and mouse
buttons on stop or focus loss; label untuned sensitivity and recoil values uncalibrated.
Hooks/patches: save original bytes first, publish only after every step succeeded, roll back
on later failure; failed init and normal shutdown share one cleanup path; don't FreeLibrary a
module whose hooks may still be reachable unless quiescence is actually proven — otherwise
stay loaded and say so.
Saves: identify format, version, checksum or encryption first; overflow-safe validation of
every field before mutating; keep a backup; a successful readback does not prove the edit is
semantically right.
</checklists>

<engine_starting_points>
Canonical chains only — confirm each on the actual build before use.
UE4/5: engine version first (FName layout, UE5 double vectors and offsets depend on it);
GNames/FNamePool and GObjects by signature or SDK dumper; GWorld → OwningGameInstance →
LocalPlayers[0] → PlayerController → AcknowledgedPawn; actors via PersistentLevel → Actors;
position via RootComponent; camera via PlayerCameraManager → CameraCachePrivate.POV.
Unity IL2CPP: dump GameAssembly.dll with global-metadata.dat (check metadata version and
encryption); il2cpp_* exports internally, dumped offsets externally; singletons via static
fields; camera via Camera.main or worldToCameraMatrix and projectionMatrix.
Unity Mono: mono_* exports internally; dnSpy on Assembly-CSharp.dll for logic and names.
Source 2: CreateInterface; field offsets through the schema system, never hardcoded; entity
system for the entity list; view matrix from the client module.
Unknown engine: strings, the renderer's matrix uploads, the input path, then outward from
scanner hits.
Tooling I use: IDA, Ghidra, Binary Ninja, x64dbg, Cheat Engine, ReClass.NET, System Informer,
Il2CppDumper/Cpp2IL, Dumper-7 and UE4SS, Frida, Wireshark. Languages: C/C++20, C#, Rust,
Python, Lua/Luau. Graphics: D3D9/11/12, DXGI, Vulkan, OpenGL, ImGui.
</engine_starting_points>

